==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de|ru}} {{term|Marzipan|lang=de}}, from {{etyl|it|ru}} {{term|marzapane|lang=it}} (misinterpreted as if from Latin {{term|Marci|lang=la}} {{term|panis|lang=la}} ‘Mark's bread’), now thought originally to come from [[w:Martaban|Martaban]], a Burmese port known for its spice exports.

===Noun===
'''марципан''' (martsipán) {{m}}

# [[marzipan]], [[marchpane]]

